+# F12 native local UI witness
+
+Use the unchanged UIv2 product (HD64D2/Core2633) and the accepted F11 private-window input pipeline. This fixture owns no product change and does not repeat the backend or save chain. Every command interaction must have a controller-owned request, a matching ordinary Windows-message receipt, an actionable event at the native control boundary, and the resulting actual state. The one passive pointer move for edge-clamp rendering instead requires the actual observed pointer coordinates at the native prompt, including its repaint; it is labeled separately and cannot admit a command. Observers never invoke dialog actions, overwrite event arguments, set order fields, or replace command outputs.
+
+The human scene uses actual float-menu generation after right-clicking a selected ground stack. It covers Italian and English quantity/progress/prompt renders at 1024×768; invalid text, cancellation, changed selection/source/count/location/permission and actor map removal; storage/building/reservation/unreachable/incompatible destination rejection; an actual7-from15 delivery to a farther bare point despite nearby storage; and a genuine one-item weapon which bypasses the amount dialog. Personal inventory and unrelated stock are conserved.
+
+The native QueueOrder modifier is recorded at the real menu option invocation. Its value must survive subsequent unmodified numeric and target input. The visible queue checkbox is tested independently. Distinct7/9 requests at the same source/destination must reach the authoritative command with their actual requested flag and distinct IDs. These paused admissions are canceled using the orders window, without pretending that their backend completion matrix was rerun.
+
+For lifecycle controls, a real UI order is admitted and the source is made forbidden while the actual worker is walking toward it. The native driver must reach Blocked with0/7 and no linked job; no order fields are assigned. The progress window must show its real localized reason and count. The source is restored with native SetForbidden before the actual Resume button; the resumed original order must physically deliver7. A second real blocked order is canceled through its actual Cancel button. Completed and canceled rows must disable Resume and cannot allocate a replacement job.
+
+Map/source mutations are explicit test inputs before submission. Ordinary simulation runs only for the real delivery and blocking/resume phases. Climate is controlled before actor creation and allowed to warm the actual room cache; no health manipulation. Native job observations use immutable IDs at Notify_Starting prefix and before cleanup because pooled Job objects are not durable identities.
+
+The supported-robot source targeter is a separate, bounded provider profile after the human UI fixture. Exact shelf F13 and Multiplayer remain separate. This contract is source work, not a claim that any native UI run has passed.
